            {
                "entry_id": "a606b5a5-660f-39b2-b2b0-7fd92a81cb89",
                "word": "paraphernal",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c78e1762-5f9b-4802-89da-c3046011b911",
                        "entry_id": "a606b5a5-660f-39b2-b2b0-7fd92a81cb89",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "paraphernaux"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "44871d72-dbd9-392e-b4f7-5a633b80378c",
                        "entry_id": "a606b5a5-660f-39b2-b2b0-7fd92a81cb89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bien propre de l’épouse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ellipsis"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c52858c-7332-4aaf-a210-06572f88497a",
                                "sense_id": "44871d72-dbd9-392e-b4f7-5a633b80378c",
                                "text": "Tenez, mon second clerc est bête comme un avantage matrimonial et capable de f...f. flanquer un coup de canif dans les paraphernaux de la future épouse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55d98763-851b-454c-9a5c-89e92992f2a5",
                                "sense_id": "44871d72-dbd9-392e-b4f7-5a633b80378c",
                                "text": "Quand miss Russel est devenue la femme de Jacques, ses paraphernaux, ses biens propres, vous comprenez, étaient de 1 500 000 francs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43d0ff2e-3b62-4ce7-926d-fffdb080d41c",
                                "sense_id": "44871d72-dbd9-392e-b4f7-5a633b80378c",
                                "text": "Enfin, en pays de droit écrit, au moins après la renaissance du droit de Justinien, la femme pouvait avoir des paraphernaux dont elle gardait la propriété, la jouissance et même l’administration."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f40b3549-a45a-4ac0-8021-69d50eab6c93",
                        "source_entry_id": "a606b5a5-660f-39b2-b2b0-7fd92a81cb89",
                        "source_sense_id": "44871d72-dbd9-392e-b4f7-5a633b80378c",
                        "target_lang_word": "parapherna",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parapherna",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "110b80ba-3a5c-3391-b72f-8beef49ec41a",
                                        "entry_id": "d05695be-2c68-346d-959e-9c237de81f48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A woman's property which was not made a part of her marriage dower, but remained her own."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient-Rome",
                                            "historical",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0bbc6138-f016-4e2b-a79a-3376269d4c3b",
                        "source_entry_id": "a606b5a5-660f-39b2-b2b0-7fd92a81cb89",
                        "source_sense_id": "44871d72-dbd9-392e-b4f7-5a633b80378c",
                        "target_lang_word": "paraphernalia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paraphernalia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14fccfb8-611e-36ea-bbc7-20af05b737fc",
                                        "entry_id": "87f5bdfd-18a4-3800-aa55-43dfc0440646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Miscellaneous items, especially the set of equipment required for a particular activity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "541daf91-94b9-4700-8e1a-881fb16928a0",
                                                "sense_id": "14fccfb8-611e-36ea-bbc7-20af05b737fc",
                                                "text": "He has an impressive collection of bicycling paraphernalia, but he doesn't ride very often anymore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d03e971-e63c-499f-b95c-b1ec5fae96d6",
                                                "sense_id": "14fccfb8-611e-36ea-bbc7-20af05b737fc",
                                                "text": "Then the boys arrived, with their camping paraphernalia, and in such bubbling good spirits that the girls were infected with them, for they had become rather lonesome of late."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04f10dd1-bcfc-496c-bcfd-d760ad3dff76",
                                                "sense_id": "14fccfb8-611e-36ea-bbc7-20af05b737fc",
                                                "text": "People such as William James and the Stephensons (with whom he collaborated) may have been the movers and shakers of the early railways, but there was other, less exalted bods who constructed all the paraphernalia - including stations."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c71e894c-c5f2-34e5-8b4a-42c797490001",
                                        "entry_id": "87f5bdfd-18a4-3800-aa55-43dfc0440646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Objects that a married woman owns, such as clothing and jewellery, apart from her dowry."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ac55967-6214-4267-bb3b-0f3e79213f7b",
                                                "sense_id": "c71e894c-c5f2-34e5-8b4a-42c797490001",
                                                "text": "So she told her what her husband had said and sat with her awhile; but, presently, up came porters, who brought all her clothes and paraphernalia and what not else belonged to her of goods and vessels from her husband’s house and deposited them in that of her mother."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
